The restServer binary gets `pkg/http/restServer/diaApi` from the published `github.com/diadata-org/diadata` module, not from the source tree. The `diaApi.go` fixes in this PR only reach the binary once a v1.4.714 tag exists that contains them.

I couldn't check three things from here:
- whether a v1.4.714 tag exists and includes this PR's `diaApi` changes;
- whether `cmd/http/restServer/go.sum` was updated;
- whether a `replace` directive exists.

If the tag or the `go.sum` entry is missing, building restServer fails. If the tag exists without these changes, the deployed API still panics with a 500 on the historic URLs. Tag the release after merging and update `go.sum` in the same change, or use a `replace`/pseudo-version that points at this commit.
